    "body": "Reviewer: Codex CLI 0.157.1, gpt-6-astra, medium effort. Head b44a3ab.\n\nReviewed issues #70–#73, the full diff, repository requirements, and PR history; there are no earlier comments or reviews to resolve. All 15 added tests, targeted Ruff checks, and both import contracts pass, and GitHub reports green CI, but the probes below expose gaps not covered by those tests. The checkout was left unchanged; the full local aggregate was not rerun in this read-only review.\n\nBlocking findings (details and resolutions inline):\n\n1. The waiter can accept an older successful check while a same-named check is queued; a pure-value probe returned `success` for that combination. Resolve check identity/ordering without treating a missing start time as an older run, and add duplicate-check regression cases.\n2. The advertised timeout does not bound GitHub subprocess calls; a one-second wait took 4.27 seconds with a stub that delayed each response by two seconds. Apply the remaining time budget to every subprocess call and test a stalled command.\n3. The shell independently filters work-item labels and transforms check data. Source inspection confirms policy duplication outside the pure core; move these pure decisions and transformations into core functions and test them with values.\n",
